            "en": "One early documented form appeared in 1734 in connection with a speech by William Wyndham. It was described as an old maxim, suggesting that the saying was already known. The proverb is often attributed to Robert Walpole, but a later account records his narrower comment, “All those men have their price,” about a particular group of politicians; the broader proverb should not be presented as his proven invention.",
